Description: use linear filtering for the feedback textures
 The motion blur and glow draw the previous frame back on a quad slightly
 smaller than the screen, so the texture is minified. With GL_NEAREST the
 rows above and below the centre are sampled from opposite sides, and the
 feedback turned this into a visible line at exactly half the height of
 the image. GL_LINEAR removes it.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
--- a/osa.c
+++ b/osa.c
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
 		glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_WRAP_T, GL_REPEAT);
 
 		glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, GL_LINEAR);
-		glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+		glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_LINEAR);
 		glTexImage2D(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0,
 		             GL_RGBA,
 		             TW,TH,
